(Bheeshm Phase 2 Proposal - Runtime Profiles) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Bheeshm Phase 2 Proposal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Runtime Profiles for ACSIL Studies) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Target environment: Quarkus + HTML frontend + SQLite3 backend) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Document date: 2026-03-15) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Objective) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Phase 2 extends Bheeshm from a calibration JSON publisher into a controlled runtime profile) Tj
T*
(publisher for ACSIL studies.) Tj
T*
(The goal is to support stable, study-specific, instrument-specific, chart-specific,) Tj
T*
(intent-specific parameter sets without exposing those values) Tj
T*
(directly in Sierra Chart study inputs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Core outcome: Bheeshm stores and publishes one approved runtime JSON file per active) Tj
T*
(profile, and the ACSIL study) Tj
T*
(loads that file locally at runtime.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Problem Statement) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Current study parameters are often embedded directly in ACSIL inputs or code. That creates) Tj
T*
(four problems:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Proprietary parameter sets are exposed to end users.) Tj
T*
(- Large studies become difficult to manage across multiple instruments, chart types, and) Tj
T*
(target intents.) Tj
T*
(- The same study may need multiple profiles for the same instrument.) Tj
T*
(- Promoting a new live parameter set is operationally harder than replacing a single) Tj
T*
(published file.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This is especially relevant for large custom studies such as K_Util_ModeBaton_V2.cpp, where) Tj
T*
(profiles can differ by) Tj
T*
(instrument, chart type, session, and target intent while remaining otherwise stable for long) Tj
T*
(periods.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Design Principles) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Keep ACSIL consumption local and file-based. Studies should not query Bheeshm directly.) Tj
T*
(- Use one JSON file per live profile, not one giant file for all studies.) Tj
T*
(- Share only minimal metadata conventions. Payload parsing remains study-specific.) Tj
T*
(- Separate calibration data from reference/runtime profile data.) Tj
T*
(- Treat profile publication as a lifecycle with draft, approved, and live states.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Scope of Phase 2) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In scope) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Metadata model for runtime profiles.) Tj
T*
(- SQLite schema for profile storage and promotion.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
