() Tj
T*
(Recommended split on the ACSIL side:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Minimal shared envelope and JSON helper utilities.) Tj
T*
(- Study-specific payload structs and loader functions.) Tj
T*
(- No repeated JSON inspection scattered across the main study logic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(13. Example Lifecycle) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- User creates or edits profile MODE_BATON / MES / 1MIN / RTH / ORB / v3.) Tj
T*
(- Bheeshm stores it as version 3 with status draft.) Tj
T*
(- User reviews and approves it.) Tj
T*
(- User publishes it to live.) Tj
T*
(- Bheeshm writes the final JSON file to the configured live folder.) Tj
T*
(- The Sierra study reads that file locally and validates the envelope.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(14. Risks and Constraints) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- If the client can access the JSON file on disk, the values are still readable. This is) Tj
T*
(operational hiding, not strong secrecy.) Tj
T*
(- Payload shapes will vary significantly by study. That is expected and should not be) Tj
T*
(over-abstracted.) Tj
T*
(- The live folder path and write permissions need to be explicitly configured in Quarkus.) Tj
T*
(- Version and status transitions should be guarded to prevent multiple live versions of the) Tj
T*
(same logical profile.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(15. Recommended First Implementation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Add the runtime_profiles and optional runtime_profile_events tables.) Tj
T*
(- Implement basic Quarkus CRUD and publish endpoints.) Tj
T*
(- Create one HTML workflow for managing runtime profiles.) Tj
T*
(- Use one large study, likely Mode Baton, as the first Phase 2 consumer.) Tj
T*
(- Keep the current calibration flow unchanged while proving the new profile flow separately.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(16. Final Recommendation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Bheeshm Phase 2 should store runtime profiles in separate SQLite tables, publish them as one) Tj
T*
(JSON file per live profile,) Tj
T*
(and keep ACSIL consumption local, typed, and study-specific. This gives operational control,) Tj
T*
(versioning, cleaner deployment,) Tj
T*
(and reduced exposure of sensitive settings in Sierra study inputs without overbuilding a) Tj
T*
(universal schema framework.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
